From 4ef2302e24334e4571968e2cd51310819959852f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hIRoic native Linux hammer <noreply@example.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 22:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sqlite: enable bounded-memory operation on NOMMU

The STM32F746 has 8 MiB of RAM and Linux cannot satisfy a large anonymous
mapping from non-contiguous pages.  SQLite's positive default asks each page
cache to allocate 20 pages in one block.  With the database's page size and
per-page metadata this becomes a roughly 68 KiB mapping, which requires an
order-5 buddy allocation and fails after lvmusic has fragmented memory.

Use SQLite's supported negative form to cap the initial bulk allocation at
16 KiB.  Also compile the MEMSYS5 allocator so the hammer helper can provide
SQLite with a fixed heap and avoid later large system allocations in VACUUM.
PRAGMA cache_size=-16 remains in the workload, so the configured cache budget
does not change.

Signed-off-by: hIRoic native Linux hammer <noreply@example.com>
---
 sqlite3.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sqlite3.c b/sqlite3.c
index d613eeb..9427cb2 100644
--- a/sqlite3.c
+++ b/sqlite3.c
@@ -15775,5 +15775,9 @@
 ** speedtest1 test program with options: --shrink-memory --reprepare
 */
+#ifndef SQLITE_ENABLE_MEMSYS5
+# define SQLITE_ENABLE_MEMSYS5 1
+#endif
+
 #ifndef SQLITE_DEFAULT_PCACHE_INITSZ
-# define SQLITE_DEFAULT_PCACHE_INITSZ 20
+# define SQLITE_DEFAULT_PCACHE_INITSZ -16
 #endif
